From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prokrypt <prokrypt@edited.us>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:03:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 36/37] image-fdt: leave room for the bootstage node

image_setup_libfdt() shrinks the device tree to its minimum size, and
announce_and_cleanup() only adds the bootstage node after that, so with
more than a few dozen records it runs out of space. The records are
written newest first, so the ones that get lost are the oldest: TPL,
SPL and the start of U-Boot proper. With CONFIG_BOOTSTAGE_FDT, keep
8 KB free.
---
 boot/image-fdt.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/boot/image-fdt.c b/boot/image-fdt.c
index f10200f6..9578e0d1 100644
--- a/boot/image-fdt.c
+++ b/boot/image-fdt.c
@@ -686,7 +686,13 @@ int image_setup_libfdt(struct bootm_headers *images, void *blob,
 		lmb_free(lmb, (phys_addr_t)(u32)(uintptr_t)blob,
 			 (phys_size_t)fdt_totalsize(blob));
 
-	ret = fdt_shrink_to_minimum(blob, 0);
+	/*
+	 * Leave room for the bootstage node, which announce_and_cleanup()
+	 * adds after this: without it the oldest records (TPL, SPL) were
+	 * the ones that didn't fit.
+	 */
+	ret = fdt_shrink_to_minimum(blob,
+				    IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_BOOTSTAGE_FDT) ? 0x2000 : 0);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		goto err;
 	of_size = ret;
-- 
